.DS_Store
tmp/
.env

# Runtime state Claude Code writes into a project's `.claude/` (settings.local.json,
# caches, session data) must never be committed — this repo is public. So deny the
# directory and re-include the tracked defaults one by one, the way `ai-setup` does it:
# present AND future runtime folders stay out of git without anyone remembering to add a
# line.
#
# These patterns carry a LEADING SLASH on purpose. `.claude/*` would be anchored to this
# file's directory by git's own rule (a separator in the middle anchors the pattern), but
# the explicit form says so out loud — `symlink/.claude/` is TRACKED MACHINERY, and an
# unanchored pattern that swallowed it would silently stop shipping every role agent,
# command and hook to every instance.
/.claude/*
!/.claude/rules/

# NOT ignored, and deliberately listed here so nobody "tidies" them into the block above:
#   symlink/.claude/**   — machinery symlinked into every instance
#   plugin/seed/.gitignore — an active .gitignore over this template's own seed directory.
#                          Never add an `/index.md` line THERE: it would match
#                          plugin/seed/index.md and stop this repo tracking its own seed
#                          file. tests/derived-indexes.test.sh holds that trap closed.

# `claude plugin eval` writes a timestamped results/ directory and an HTML report under
# the eval dir on every run. Run artifacts, never sources — and this repo is public, so
# a transcript of a model run is not something to commit by accident.
/plugin/evals/results/
